REPAIRAGENT-OCI THOUGHTS: [0m The key failing path is src/libcrun/container.c:do_hooks. Hook execution returns the hook process exit status as a positive value, and the caller propagates that positive value. crun's error reporting paths generally surface libcrun_error_t diagnostics for negative error returns; returning the raw positive hook exit status can therefore drop details captured by run_process_with_stdin_timeout_envp, including hook stderr. A focused fix is to preserve the existing generic log but normalize a non-keep-going hook failure to a negative libcrun-style error return so any captured stderr in err is retained and reported by the runtime. I will insert an explanatory comment above the changed behavior and validate with the build via write_fix.
